  "mechanisms": [
    "SSH verifies registered private-key possession before the subsystem receives a typed tenant/partner/actor principal. Every operation rechecks the active key and frozen authority revision.",
    "Key enrollment/revocation commits exact immutable public-key events with the registry transition; revoked keys cannot be re-enrolled by retry. Local administrative references remain required.",
    "Receive into a separate generated revision. Track at most 1024 merged byte ranges; missing packets and disconnected unclosed handles cannot publish. Seal/sync before atomic file/path/journal/receipt commit.",
    "Retain old immutable revisions on overwrite; preserve uncertain sealed bytes and crash orphans for read-only reconciliation.",
    "Read through the exact verified descriptor and recheck current mount/mode/key/account permission for each bounded read.",
    "Validate frame length before allocation, preserve raw-path validation before library cleaning, process one packet per response, cap packets, handles, writers and session time.",
    "Reject shell, forwarding, links, ownership/extension attributes and unsupported protocol semantics explicitly.",
    "The SSH transport owns normal channel status/closure. The SFTP library may abort a failing channel, but normal cleanup preserves the final exit-status exchange.",
    "Invalid current authority closes active transfer sessions promptly; the original rate-limited eight-second revocation test passes without extending its budget."
  ],
